Title: The Quiet Ledger
Author: pipeline

INT. COUNTY RECORDS OFFICE - DAY

A ledger lies open on the table. Dust drifts through the window light.
A clerk turns a brittle page. [SRC: Montana Plaindealer, 13 April 1906]

CLERK
The entry was never signed.

EXT. RAIL DEPOT - DUSK

An empty platform. A single suitcase stands abandoned near the tracks.
A newspaper page is pinned beneath it. [SRC: The River Press, 22 April 1903]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
According to the archived record, the inquiry was opened that spring.

EXT. COURTHOUSE STEPS - DAY

A map of the county is unfolded across the stone wall.
Handwritten notes cover the margin in faded ink. [SRC: loc.gov, 1903]
